<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Release-scoped upgrade data for Darpan 1.5.0 (DAR-BE-005 — shared config across tenants).
Records must also live in generic source data files under runtime/component/darpan/data/.
Load with: ./gradlew loadDarpanUpgradeData

ORDERING: hand-verified parent-before-child — EnumerationType precedes its Enumerations.
release_preflight.py sorts alphabetically and WILL break this if the file is regenerated; re-order
by hand afterwards.

OPERATOR IMPACT: five additive records, no behaviour change. Until they load, no config can be
shared, because a grant must name a configTypeEnumId that exists. Nothing existing is modified, so
loading this file changes no current reconciliation behaviour.

NO BACKFILL — DELIBERATE (Aditi, 2026-08-12). An earlier draft of this file also carried a one-time
ConfigTenantAccess row pre-sharing a HotWax OMS config between two named tenants. It was dropped:
sharing is granted through the product, not through a data file. A tenant admin uses the "Shared
with" panel (facade.ConfigSharingFacadeServices.grant#ConfigTenantAccess), which requires them to
be tenant-admin of BOTH the target tenant and a tenant already using the config — the two-sided
gate. Pre-seeding a grant meant baking three unverified production tenant/config ids into a release
artifact to save a few clicks, and a row naming the wrong tenant would silently widen access to that
tenant's operators. The product path has no such failure mode.

Consequently this file is safe to load unconditionally and needs no verification step.

SETUP NOTE for whoever shares a config: the two-sided gate means the acting user must hold
DARPAN_TENANT_ADMIN in both tenants. That is a permissions assignment in the admin app, not a code
or data change. Both tenants must also live in the SAME deployment — ConfigTenantAccess is a row in
one database referencing tenants in that same database, so tenants on separate instances cannot
share a config by any mechanism.

PREREQUISITE: 1.4.0 upgrade-data must be loaded first.
-->
<entity-facade-xml type="darpan-seed">

    <!-- Config-type catalog. Adding a value here plus a CONFIG_TYPE_REGISTRY row in
         SharedConfigAccessSupport is the whole extension path for a new shareable config type.
         moqui.service.message.SystemMessageRemote is deliberately absent: it is a framework-owned
         endpoint descriptor already visible to every tenant, not a per-tenant credential. -->
    <moqui.basic.EnumerationType enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"
            description="Darpan API source config types that support cross-tenant sharing"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SCFG_HOTWAX_OMS"
            description="HotWax OMS REST source config (darpan.hotwax.HotWaxOmsRestSourceConfig)"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SCFG_SHOPIFY_AUTH"
            description="Shopify auth config (darpan.shopify.ShopifyAuthConfig)"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SCFG_NS_AUTH"
            description="NetSuite auth config (darpan.reconciliation.NsAuthConfig)"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SCFG_NS_RESTLET"
            description="NetSuite Restlet config (darpan.reconciliation.NsRestletConfig)"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"/>

</entity-facade-xml>
